            <h2 class="margin-top-2">Group Registration</h2>
            <p>Group registration is available for organizations registering 15 or more attendees. Eligible registrants receive a flat registration rate. In-person Registration: $955.00 Virtual Registration: $725.00</p>

            <h2 id="payments">Payments</h2>
            <p>Credit cards, wire transfer and checks, all in USD, are accepted forms of payment. To ensure secure and timely receipt of payments, checks will only be accepted if delivered via one of the following approved shipping methods: DHL, FedEx UPS, USPS Ground or Priority Mail (with tracking). Checks sent through any other delivery method or without tracking will not be accepted.</p>

            <p><strong>Please note:</strong> Paying the abstract submission fee does not constitute registration for the meeting. Registration submitted without full payment cannot be processed and attendees will not be registered until full payment is completed. Government or other purchase orders cannot be accepted. There are no daily or partial registrations rates available.</p>

            <p>If paying by check, please make payable to:</p>
            <address>
                UTHSCSA – SABCS<br>
                UT Health San Antonio Mays Cancer Center<br>
                7979 Wurzbach Road, MC 7980<br>
                San Antonio, TX 78229-3900
            </address>

            <h2 id="ut-health-faculty-staff">UT Health San Antonio Faculty and Staff</h2>
            <p>Register and pay with your credit card, then reach out to your department for reimbursement. No IDTs will be needed this year.</p>

            <h2 id="cancellation-policy">Cancellation Policy</h2>
            <p>Cancellations must be received in writing prior to November 20, 2026, and are subject to the following processing fees:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Regular Registration, AACR Members, and UT Health San Antonio Faculty and Staff: <strong>$75.00</strong></li>
                <li>Residents/Postdoctoral Fellows and Students: <strong>$20.00</strong></li>
            </ul>
            <p>Refunds will not be granted after November 21, 2025, nor will they be granted for no-shows. Please email cancellation notices to <a href="mailto:sabcs-support@cmrus.com">SABCS® Customer Support</a>.</p>

            <h2 id="patient-advocates">Patient Advocates</h2>
            <p>This special registration category is reserved for individuals who work or volunteer for nonprofit 501(c)(3) patient advocacy organizations with a clear charitable mission focused on cancer patient support and advocacy. Attendees with five or more years of research/laboratory or clinical experience, those currently providing clinical care, or individuals working for industry are not eligible for this special rate.</p>
            <p>During registration, please upload an attestation verifying your role as a patient advocate. The attestation should include:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>A brief overview of the affiliated patient advocacy organization</li>
                <li>A description of past and current cancer-related patient advocacy work</li>
                <li>A summary of priorities and goals as a patient advocate</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 id="fraudulent-websites">Notice: Beware of Fraudulent Registration and Housing Websites</h2>
            <p>Hotel room and meeting registration pirating is a practice carried out by third-party companies that act as travel agencies, wholesalers, or destination management companies to solicit attendees for room reservations for other organizations’ meetings.</p>
            <p>Deceptive tactics used by pirate registration and housing companies include:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Adding processing fees or taxes when registering for the meeting and requiring payment via PayPal</li>
                <li>Illegally using SABCS® name and/or logo to falsely represent themselves as being affiliated with SABCS®</li>
                <li>Informing attendees and exhibitors that the SABCS® hotel room block is sold out and that if you do not book with them immediately, you may not get a room</li>
                <li>Distributing forms or promotional materials that appear to be issued by SABCS®</li>
                <li>Non-delivery of promises to customers (e.g., when customers arrive, reservations are sometimes non-existent, or the hotels are not conveniently located)</li>
                <li>Registration and hotel rates higher than those on the SABCS® website</li>
            </ul>
            <p>If you are contacted by someone asking if you need a room for the SABCS®, and the individual is not a representative of UT Health San Antonio or AACR, please get as much information as you can about the company and contact the SABCS® office.</p>
